  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Snow showers and freezing drizzle continue in\nthe Alleghenies overnight. \n\nCameras continue to show snow showers with some freezing drizzle\nacross the Alleghenies. This will continue through about sunrise\nas moisture slowly erodes. Elsewhere, mostly cloudy skies are \nexpected overnight, with overnight lows in the 30s to lower 40s.\n\nResidual clouds should tend to break up over the course of the \nday, leading to a fair amount of sunshine by this afternoon. \nWinds will be gusty out of the west, but temperatures will run a\nbit warmer, with highs in the mid to upper 50s for most \n(30s/40s mountains).\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...A cold front brings back precipitation & gusty \nwinds Sunday night into Monday, followed by drier conditions early \nnext week. \n\nHigh pressure will keep the region dry Sunday. Temperatures will be \nnear seasonable with highs middle 50s to lower 60s. \n\nShortwave upper-level ridging slides offshore late Sunday as a deep \nupper-level trough forms over the Midwest before tracking through \nthe Mid-Atlantic late Sunday & into Monday. This will produce a \nstrong cold front that will bring back the chance for areawide rain \nshowers as well as wintry precipitation across the Alleghenies \nbeginning Sunday night through Monday morning. Total QPF at this \ntime ranges between 0.25\"-0.75\" as it quickly traverses the region. \nAs the low tracks offshore Monday, winds will again become gusty \ncreating blustery conditions, possibly gusting up to 35-40 knots at \ntimes. These should quickly diminish starting late Monday & into \nTuesday as the low quickly transitions offshore, with temperatures \nfalling a bit in the wake of the cold front. Afternoon highs on \nTuesday fall to the 40s to low-50s, with overnight lows largely \nranging in the 20s to low-30s. \n\nLooking towards the rest of the week, surface high pressure \ntransitions in overhead with zonal flow reigning in the upper \nlevels. This should bring drier & calmer conditions to the region, \nwith southerly winds generally remaining light and temperatures \ngradually increasing back into the upper 50s as the week goes\non.",
